<title>PERU: Peru allows pension funds to invest in its Bradies.</title>
<headline>Peru allows pension funds to invest in its Bradies.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Peruvian Central Reserve Bank said it would allow private pension administrators to invest up to five percent of their funds in the nation's newly-issued Brady bonds.</p>
<p>The five private funds, known by their Spanish acronym AFPs, have accumulated $1.33 billion from their 1.66 million contributors in four years of operation, according to government figures.</p>
<p>The measure was announced four months after Peru finalized its restructuring of debt with private foreign banks through a Brady plan deal.</p>
<p>((-- Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
